Then you are sillier than I thought when I first saw you.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.240
Robber's daughter!

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.780
In the fog,

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.700
Ronja, who had fallen victim to the temptation of the unearthly ones,

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.920
was rescued by Birk.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.710
She had absolutely no memory of what had happened.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.760
But, Ronja felt...

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:05.480
Fall Descends on the Forest

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:05.480
Fall Descends on the Forest

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.500
I wonder how long it will take for Mattis to drive the Borkas out...

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.120
And that dirty devil...

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.680
What's he up to over there?

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.610
Today you're going scouting.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.360
Yesterday you also went scouting.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.450
And the day before that you also went scouting!

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.170
Every single day you go scouting!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.700
How about using your head a little?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:08.930
Uh-huh?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.710
If you have the time to sit there and mock me, at least spend it helping Lovis with the chores, old man.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:19.970
That sounds like it would be much more backbreaking work than a fight with Borka, doesn't it?

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.300
Let's head out!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.530
It's really quiet.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.250
This doesn't seem like a place you would find Borka robbers at all.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.620
They're here.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.710
They have no other choice but to enter the castle from here.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.220
But, we've never even seen them once, right?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.720
In that case, we'll just have to force them out!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.180
Alright. Do it!

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.520
Boss!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.370
It's fine. We won't be seen if we enter this way.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.480
Uh-huh.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.380
Boss...

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.880
Don't worry. This time we're using two ladders.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.760
It'll have no problem reaching the other side.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.640
It's not very stable...

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.650
No! Pull it up!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.360
It's caught on the roof!

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.160
What are you doing! Pull it back!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.080
We can't! It's stuck and won't budge!

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.800
Help me!

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:12.110
Every plan you've come up with so far has failed miserably.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:17.200
You'll have to be as cunning as a fox.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:21.290
Because force just doesn't seem to be working, does it?

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:29.130
At this rate, it seems like it'll be a long time before we go back to robbing people.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:34.470
We're not the only ones, Borka's robbers haven't robbed anyone either since they came here.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:39.730
Robber's road has become the safest road to travel nowadays.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.460
I've noticed that it's pretty calm.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.430
What happened to those robbers?

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.180
Ten years have passed since then.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:21.640
The forest, animals... and even robbers happen to change with time.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:29.290
Maybe they took a nap somewhere, after being intoxicated by our splendid music.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.820
If you value your life, leave your possessions now, and run.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.700
Oh, help me!

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.000
Hey!

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.290
There's nobody here!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.280
We can't find Borka's robbers anywhere!

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.830
Yeah!

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:32.800
I guess that means we can finally leave this forest.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.970
What about the robbers stationed over <i>there</i> ?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:41.510
There is no place as horrible as that castle...

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:44.850
Catching the robber chieftain that lives there

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.470
would be more difficult than catching an eagle on a clifftop.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.030
Winter is coming.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.400
Let's retreat for the year.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:16.300
They have to be here. This is the only way to enter the castle.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:28.230
You've finally shown your faces, you dirty devils!

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.180
This is nothing!

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.680
Pass me some of that.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.400
Why are you whimpering like a baby?

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:19.990
Keep still for two or three days with this on, and you'll feel better in no time.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:20.700
Aye.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.910
Hey, Lill-Klippen.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.000
What?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:34.540
Was there a kid with the Borka robbers you saw?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:39.590
Kid? You mean Borka's snake-spawn?

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:40.510
Uh-huh.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.980
No, I didn't see any snake-spawn.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:46.680
I was too busy watching the stones and arrows hail down on top of us!

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.890
Even {/i1}I{/i0} couldn't dodge them all!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.520
They sure are dirty devils!

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.460
They won't get away with it next — Oww...

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.820
I see...

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.610
You've been scouting so many times,

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.700
and the only thing you've managed to learn

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:09.830
is that the rope ladder is lowered only under strict guard?

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:16.920
Idiot!

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.840
It's so soft!

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.960
What a beautiful sound.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.960
It even smells good.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.030
Wild horses.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:35.390
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:35.390
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.930
This is so boring.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:15.930
My body goes numb on days like this when there's nothing to do!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.940
I wonder what's for dinner tonight...

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.940
Mutton soup would be good, wouldn't it?

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:28.940
Nah, chicken soup is definitely better.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:32.950
No, chicken is oily and tastes bad.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:34.410
What?!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.700
Mutton smells bad and is hard to chew!

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.460
What?!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.460
Wanna fight?!

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.090
Very well!

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.960
Stop it. What a dumb thing to fight over.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.840
What do you mean dumb?!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.150
You can't even taste anything! Stay out of this old man!

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.140
What?! Who are you calling an old man?!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:59.640
Stop it, you three. How stupid...

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.140
What do you mean by stupid?!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:04.150
If you think this is stupid, then you're the one who's stupid!

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.320
What?! You wanna fight?!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:10.650
Stop it. How childish...

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.990
Shut up, you child.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.620
That's right, you came back crying after getting by beaten by Borka!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.580
What?! You don't even have any eyebrows!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.660
And you're just a lazy watchman, Tjorm!

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.500
It's an important job, you know!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.170
Don't laugh! I'll make you spread manure on the fields!

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.840
Manure is very useful.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.470
What do you think you have to thank for the fact that you can eat vegetables?

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:41.520
I like chicken, mutton, and vegetables....

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.350
Shut up you freeloader!

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.540
Cut it out already!

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:13.550
You'll burst my eardrum soon with all that wrangling and nagging.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.880
If you guys can't get along,

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:18.300
I hope you all fall into Hell's Gap and never come back!

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.640
My nose is going to fall off!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.450
This might be karma for talking bad about chicken soup.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.420
I think we've done enough now, right?

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:55.920
I swear to the devil, I won't quibble about mutton soup from now on.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.890
He says he understands.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.870
You guys! We're going deer hunting!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.910
Hooray!

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:38.430
And now, the salting is done.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.610
Let's smoke the rest.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:45.990
If we do that, we won't have to worry about food during the winter.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:50.540
Chicken soup, mutton soup, and rice porridge don't serve a man long.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:54.040
Now we'll have something to chew on.

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:59.010
And the tenderest bits go to the toothless.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.430
As everyone knows.

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:40.840
Hey daddy!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:49.060
Someday, I'll catch a wild horse and tame it, just like you did!

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:54.190
Yes, when the time comes and you're strong enough to catch one yourself.

00:20:54.860 --> 00:20:57.690
Yes, someday I will, for sure!

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:27.050
The woods are strangely deserted.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:32.390
Where did all the animals and strange creatures run off to?

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:35.350
And that dirty devil...

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:38.060
Even though he said "It's my forest!"...

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.460
Human here...

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:49.030
Gray dwarves all... Human here...

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:46.070
Ah-choo.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:51.080
Fly off back to the pits of hell!

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:54.310
Ronja didn't meet with Birk even once during the fall.

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:58.850
That of course, made her glad.

00:22:58.850 --> 00:22:59.310
But...

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:03.320
But, is that really true?

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:13.000
Ronja was sometimes not sure how she felt.

